{
  "name": "Shadow Mode Portraits",
  "description": "Full Sonic<->Shadow identity swap in creatures.GDA. Creature 0 (the starting character) becomes Shadow in name, 3D model, stats, progression curve, POW moves and movement abilities; creature 4 becomes Sonic. Story recruitment then handles itself by symmetry - where Chapter 4 normally grants Shadow it now grants Sonic, so no plot-flag editing is needed. Dialogue portrait prefixes (columns 17/18) are deliberately NOT swapped: the engine derives portrait names from a prefix plus an expression suffix, and the two characters share only 3 of ~10 expressions, so swapping them corrupts conversation art in both directions. Structural columns (id, playerid, class) are also left alone so party slots stay intact. THIS VARIANT ALSO REMAPS DIALOGUE PORTRAITS. Rather than swapping the column-17 prefixes (which would request art that does not exist), it swaps the image payloads underneath them: PRTL_SONIC* receives Shadow art and PRTL_SDW* receives Sonic art, every frame being an identical 64x64 8bpp 4160-byte NCGR. Shadow has only 4 expressions against Sonic's 10, so six of Sonic's slots reuse the nearest of those four - nothing corrupts, Shadow is simply less expressive. PRTL_SHD is Shade, not Shadow, and is deliberately not used as a source. Column 18 (palette) follows the pixels for all four PRTL_SDW rows. Known side effect: Super Sonic (row 68) shares the PRTL_SONIC prefix and so also shows Shadow's face. Rows 75/77/116 (the story/boss \"Shadow the Hedgehog\" encounters) have namestrref repointed to 14286 \"Sonic the Hedgehog\" so their name matches the portrait they now show. This is a repoint rather than a TLK edit because strrefs 21865/21867 share their string bytes with a third entry (14279) and editing in place would corrupt it. ALSO RETARGETS combo.GDA. Each POW move names the creature id that owns it (column 2) and up to three partner ids (columns 3-5). Those are creature ids, not names, so after the swap every Shadow move still demanded creature 4 - which on a fresh game is not recruited - and all six greyed out as \"You do not have the characters required\", including the solo moves. Columns 2-5 therefore have 0 and 4 exchanged wherever they appear, which also fixes the Knuckles duos (rows 8-11) and Blade Drop (row 57) that name Sonic or Shadow as a partner.",
